                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "While it is still in Early Access, and there are some quirks here and there, Venture Forth holds a lot of promise in regards to being a top-notch 3d adventure game! It gives as much as it takes, and believe me, while there will be some moments of frustration, there's also a lot to love about the game in general.\n\nI really like the feeling of being in some underground lava caverns with who-knows-what. Small thoughts creep into your heart from time to time (Or at the top left) about locating the heart, finding the center, and every so often settling on despair. It's a nice, subtle poke in the side that urges you on.\n\nVarious areas are often hiding something, whether it's an item you need to continue forward or an over-powered weapon, the key to the game is to kill everything and explore everything, and to always check your inventory for special items that have dropped.  It feels like an adventure game that caters mostly to the inquisitive folk that want to explore every nook and cranny of an area. While I can't say I'm the same and I have gotten stuck on more than one occasion, I also wouldn't change the way a player progresses through the game. Some clues might be nice though!\n\nThe music is ambient, and I kind of wish there were a few more tracks, but I haven't reached the end of the game yet, so I don't know how long it takes to beat it.\n\nThe monsters are adorable, and I'd hug them to bits if they didn't hit me with arrows or bumrush me so much!\n\nAs mentioned before, there are some quirks here and there. I really had (and still do), have a bit of a time understanding the inventory system. It's fully customizable, but for new players who don't have many items in the first place, I haven't seen the need for so many slots and bars. Aaand maybe some more whispered clues when a player is stuck and doesn't know what to do or what to look for. I'm a sucky adventurer though, so that might just be me!\n\nOverall, I really like this game and definitely recommend checking it out.",
